Establishment of a K-8 public lab school. 25LSO-0195, 1.0
FISCAL NOTE
FY 2026 FY 2027 FY 2028
NON-ADMINISTRATIVE IMPACT
Anticipated Expenditure increase
PUBLIC SCHOOL FOUNDATION PROGRAM ACCOUNT $2,500,000 $2,000,000 $1,100,000
Source of expenditure increase:
This bill creates a K-8 public lab school on the main campus of the University of
Wyoming that would be part of the resident school district, Albany County School
District No. 1, not to exceed 200 students beginning school year 2025-2026. The
creation of this school would increase funding through the K-12 education resource
block grant model's (K-12 funding model) foundation program guarantee amount.
The estimated impact to the K-12 funding model’s foundation program guarantee is
an increase of $2,500,000 in FY 2026, $2,000,000 in FY 2027, and $1,100,000 in FY
2028. An increase to the K-12 funding model’s foundation program guarantee amount
will have a corresponding expenditure increase from the Public School Foundation
Program Account in the form of school district entitlement payments.
Assumptions:
The above estimates were determined through the use of forecast K-12 funding models
utilized by the Legislative Service Office and Wyoming Department of Education and
are based on the most recent available data. The estimates assume that this school
is funded as a charter school as required under W.S. 21-17-504 as created by this
bill and has an enrollment of 200 students.
The University of Wyoming indicates this bill creates an indeterminable and
significant administrative impact.
